TITLE:: Hall
summary:: a concert hall reverb: a modulated Dattorro tank with early reflections and a pre-delay, as a UGen and as an object, with a window
categories:: Libraries>Reverbs
related:: Classes/FxParamUnit, Classes/HallView, Classes/ReverbView, Classes/ReverbKit, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxChain

DESCRIPTION::
A concert hall: the input diffused into a modulated Dattorro tank, with early reflections and a pre-delay; slow to build, long, moving. One of the four reverbs of the sc-reverbs extension, with link::Classes/Hall::, link::Classes/Plate::, link::Classes/Coil:: and link::Classes/Shimmer::.

code::
Ndef(\keys, { Hall.ar(Blip.ar([220, 221], 8) * Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(0.5), 0.01, 0.2) * 0.3, \hall) }).play;

h = Hall(Ndef(\keys), \hall);
h.gui;
h.decay = 6; h.room = 1.6; h.preDelay = 0.04;
h.preset = \cathedral;
::

The input goes through a pre-delay, then four allpasses that smear it, into a tank of two branches in a figure of eight: each branch is an allpass whose time moves a little (modDepth, modRate), a delay, the damping, another allpass and a second delay, feeding the other branch. room scales every delay in it. decay is the time the tail takes to fall 60 dB whatever the room: the loop gain is worked out from the lap. damp is a low pass in the loop, so the high end dies first, as in a real room, and lowCut a high pass so the bottom does not pile up. Five early reflections a side, before the tail, at early.

The tank's first output arrives about 170 ms after the input at a room of 1, so with early at 0 a short sound has a gap before its tail; the reflections fill it.

subsection:: The object and the UGen
It is an link::Classes/FxParamUnit::, so everything that class documents works here: code::Hall.ar(in, name)::, code::Hall(node, name)::, code::Hall.onBus(bus, numChannels)::, presets, the clipboard, code::gui::. Its window (link::Classes/FxDeviceGUI::) shares a frame with the other reverbs and draws its own space in its own colour: the display is a link::Classes/HallView:: (the onset beside the tail; the gestures are in link::Classes/ReverbView::). In SuperDirtGUI it is the insert kind code::\hall::.

The UGen takes any number of channels: one channel is fed to both sides of the reverb and gets the middle of them back; more than two are read as the first and the last, and every channel gets a side.

subsection:: Parameters
Each is a property of the object: read it, set it. The numbers are in the order of the node's control, which is what saved node maps carry.

table::
## strong::parameter:: || strong::range:: || strong::default:: || strong::what it does::
## code::preDelay:: || 0 .. 0.25 s || 0.02 || the gap before the reverb starts - or drag its edge in the display
## code::room:: || 0.3 .. 3 x || 1 || how big the hall is: the tank's delays, scaled - a bigger one swells later
## code::decay:: || 0.2 .. 60 s || 2.5 || how long the tail takes to fall 60 dB - or drag the tail's end
## code::diffusion:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.7 || how smeared the input is on its way in: low is echoey, high is smooth
## code::early:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.4 || how loud the first reflections are, off the walls, before the tail
## code::damp:: || 500 .. 20000 Hz || 6000 || the low pass in the loop: the high end dies first
## code::lowCut:: || 20 .. 1000 Hz || 60 || the high pass in the loop: keeps the bottom from piling up
## code::modDepth:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.3 || how much the tank's allpasses move: thickens the tail, chorus at the top
## code::modRate:: || 0.1 .. 3 Hz || 0.7 || how fast they move
## code::width:: || 0 .. 2 || 1 || how far apart the two sides are: 0 is mono
## code::mix:: || 0 .. 1 || 0.3 || how much of the effect goes out, against the dry signal
## code::output:: || -36 .. 24 dB || 0 || the level of the whole thing, in dB
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: viewKeys
What the plain link::Classes/ReverbView:: draws and drags (the face uses it for its readout): an Event naming the parameters that are the decay, the pre-delay (nil when there is none) and the damping, with the damping's range.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\keys, { Hall.ar(Blip.ar([220, 221], 8) * Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(0.5), 0.01, 0.2) * 0.3, \hall) }).play;

h = Hall(Ndef(\keys), \hall);
h.gui;
h.decay = 6; h.room = 1.6; h.preDelay = 0.04;
h.preset = \cathedral;
h.preset = Hall.presetNames.choose;
h.free; Ndef(\keys).clear;
::
